# headwear/collar/angular: the forge collar `angular` (STYLE_P2 28.3, contracts 3c: overlay collar.<v>, anchor neck, rigid)
# KNAPPED: standing shards of black glass beside the jaw and a sawtooth of points round the neck, each lit on its left facet.
# Written by the FORGE-HELM area's tools/gen.py from src/ (the hand-drawn D U R views; L is R re-lit). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (FORGE-HEAD i1, tools/collar.py) cut to 2 rows below the neck line (STYLE_P2 28.3): it no longer lays over the chest motif.
# (FORGE-HEAD envelope r2) facing L the lit row starts a step darker: the head hides its neighbours there, leaving a lone 1 px glint (C19 A8)
# (envelope fix round, HEAD, D59) the band under the jaw one dark glass plane (steps 1-2) in every facing, lit only at its
# top-left end: the pale bar no longer crosses the lower face facing R / L; the light stays on the standing shards
